envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-schema-context
type: schema
id: context
context: lib/node-schemas — shared node-type schema registry
intent: null
summary: null
system: null
tags: []
exported_at: 1794200000000
source: nexus.lib.node-export
payload:
  status: REAL
  source: >-
    Added 2026-11-09. James: "i meant the data that runs through the pipeline like idearium pipeline does, emerge, .contracts with .dag, .chunk,
    .context or any of the nodes." · "look at the idearium pipeline, don't limit to just my request for the node types". The request spine
    (docs/2026-10-12-request-spine-phasemap.spec RQ7_the_context_obligations) asks every source at once for what a request needs; nothing kept that
    answer as a node: the type was missing from this directory. A .context is what a step was given to work from: each item with where it came
    from, and each obligation found or left as a gap (an unfound fact is a named gap, never a guess: M1). Written by cos/pipeline/runs.eg into a
    request's nodes/; read by the next step and its gate.
  fields:
    for:
      type: string
      required: true
      description: what this context is for — a request id, or <request>.<step>
    items:
      type: list
      required: true
      description: "[{ source (the system or node it came from), ref (its id or path), text (what was taken, or a summary), cites? }]"
    obligations:
      type: list
      required: false
      description: "[{ need (what must be known), status: found | gap, source? }] — RQ7's checklist; a gap is asked, never guessed"
    hash:
      type: string
      required: false
      description: sha256 of the items, so a step can say exactly which context it ran on
